,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-04-27T17:15:03Z","updated_at":"2025-04-28T15:10:37Z","closed_at":"2025-04-28T15:09:40Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105837","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105837","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105837.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105837.patch","merged_at":"2025-04-28T15:09:40Z"},"body":"Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105783 (I think)\r\n\r\nI was not able to reproduce the shader compilation error in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105783. But looking at the error it complains about comparing a float and a const int using `>=`. `>=` is only used in one place in the sky shader and it was indeed comparing between a float and a const int. \r\n\r\nNotably, some strict GLSL implementations will not convert `0` to a float in a comparison and require users to be extremely explicit. I tested https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101973 on a MacBook which has a less strict GLSL implementation, so no error was produced. \r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.g